# 30. ACCOUNTING RULES — CRITICAL

Do not break existing accounting logic.

## Income

Regular earned or received income contributes to income totals.

## Expenses

Actual spending contributes to expense totals.

## Transfers

Transfers between a user's own accounts do not increase income or expenses.

## Loans

Loan received increases available funds but is not earned income.

## Udhar

Money borrowed is not income.

Money lent is not an expense.

## Repayments

Repayment received reduces receivable.

Repayment paid reduces payable.

Do not count repayment as new income or expense incorrectly.

## Refunds

Refunds must be classified and accounted for correctly to avoid inflating income.

## Savings goals

Internal savings allocations must not incorrectly duplicate cash or account balances.

All financial totals across Dashboard, Transactions, Accounts, Reports and Analytics must reconcile.

